  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Afternoon through next Friday) \nIssued at 127 PM CDT Fri Jul 17 2026\n\nFor Saturday afternoon, a weekend low pressure system will still \nremain across eastern New Mexico and northwestern Texas. This will\nbe enough support for a low chance (30%) of an isolated rain \nshower or thunderstorm. This will be for locations that are \nacross areas to the west of a Haskell to Robert Lee line. Then for\nSunday, another round of potential isolated rain showers will be \nin place for those same locations. \n\nBy early next week, high pressure starts to make a return across\nthe region. Hotter and drier weather is then expected to settle\nacross the region. High temperatures will make a return to the\nupper 90s and triple digits.",
